### 🔍 Linear Search

Linear Search is a simple searching technique where we check each element of an array one by one until the target element is found.

* Start from the first element of the array.
* Compare each element with the target value.
* If a match is found, return its index.
* If the entire array is checked and the target is not found, return `-1`.

**Time Complexity:** `O(n)`
**Space Complexity:** `O(1)`

### Solution

class Solution {
    public int linearSearch(int nums[], int target) {
		//Your code goes here
        int index=-1;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++)
        {
            if(target==nums[i]) 
            {
                index=i;
                break;
            }
        }
        return index;
    }
}
